{% comment %}
  FUEL_04 variant announcement row. Rendered inside the offer-timebar link,
  between the top banner and the control offer row, and shipped hidden. With
  the variant class on, assets/fuel04-multibuy.css hides the control row and
  the white mobile icon strip and shows this row in their place, inside the
  same link.

  What changes against control: the sale label and the countdown go away on
  both breakpoints and one uppercase offer line takes their place, with an
  outline gift glyph either side of it. The payment icons stay, drawn here
  rather than by the control row, so the strip below the bar can go away with
  the row it belongs to.

  Frame 127:70044 is the target: 1440 x 56, #17803d, white type, glyph 20.28 x
  20 either side, icon strip 32 tall. The colours are the frame's and live in
  the stylesheet, not in the section settings. The row this one replaces sits
  on secondary_color and writes in primary_color, and on this store that pair
  is pale mint with dark green ink, which is the design inverted.

  The line is a section setting, not a literal. The offer changed once already
  (percentage ladder to gift with purchase, 2026-08-27) and the final Swedish
  wording is still coming from Korana, so it has to be changeable in the theme
  editor without a deploy. The default is the string the brief and the frame
  both carry. The second line is empty by default because the frame has one
  line; it is kept so a second can be added without a deploy.

  Swedish market only, like the rest of the test.

  Accepts:
  - section: {Object} the hosting offer-timebar section, for its settings and
    payment icon blocks (required)
{% endcomment %}
{%- if request.locale.iso_code == 'sv' -%}
  {%- capture fuel04_glyph -%}
    <svg
      class="fuel04-bar__glyph"
      width="20.28"
      height="20"
      viewBox="0 0 20.28 20"
      fill="none"
      stroke="currentColor"
      stroke-width="1"
      stroke-linecap="round"
      stroke-linejoin="round"
      aria-hidden="true"
      focusable="false">
      <rect x="1.14" y="6.5" width="18" height="3.5" rx="0.75" />
      <path d="M2.64 10v8.25a.75.75 0 0 0 .75.75h13.5a.75.75 0 0 0 .75-.75V10" />
      <path d="M10.14 6.5V19" />
      <path d="M10.14 6.5S9.1 1 6.4 1a2.2 2.2 0 0 0 0 5.5z" />
      <path d="M10.14 6.5s1.04-5.5 3.74-5.5a2.2 2.2 0 0 1 0 5.5z" />
    </svg>
  {%- endcapture -%}
  <div class="fuel04-v fuel04-bar" style="display: none;">
    <div class="fuel04-bar__inner">
      {%- if section.settings.fuel04_line != blank or section.settings.fuel04_sub != blank -%}
        <div class="fuel04-bar__group">
          {{ fuel04_glyph }}
          <div>
            {%- if section.settings.fuel04_line != blank -%}
              <p class="fuel04-bar__copy">{{ section.settings.fuel04_line }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if section.settings.fuel04_sub != blank -%}
              <p class="fuel04-bar__sub">{{ section.settings.fuel04_sub }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
          {{ fuel04_glyph }}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
        <div class="fuel04-bar__icons">
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              The control row leaves width empty on these, which gives the
              browser no aspect ratio to reserve and moves the header while the
              icons load. Here the width is computed from the image so the row
              keeps its height from the first paint, and a block with no image
              picked draws nothing rather than a broken one.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if block.settings.icon != blank -%}
              {%- assign fuel04_icon_w = block.settings.icon.aspect_ratio | times: 36 | round -%}
              <img
                class="fuel04-bar__icon"
                src="{{ block.settings.icon | image_url: height: 108 }}"
                height="36"
                width="{{ fuel04_icon_w }}"
                alt="{{ block.settings.label | escape }}">
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
